{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/mediation",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "mediation"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "A voluntary and confidential procedure in which an impartial third party, with no decision-making power, helps the parties to a dispute to reach an agreement by themselves."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "Under the CRPD, mediation must be accessible and have the procedural accommodations and supports needed for the person with a disability to participate on an equal basis, with their legal capacity recognised and without substitution of their will (arts. 9, 12 and 13). It also has an essential limit: art. 48 of the Istanbul Convention prohibits mandatory mediation in cases of violence against women or domestic violence, a caution that is especially relevant where disability and dependency coincide."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "10.5"
  ],
  "narrower": [
    {
